message.content:
Sure! Below is a **sample JSON specification** for a hypothetical “Startup Stats” API that lets you query startup data such as funding, industry, location, and growth metrics.

```json
{
  "name": "Startup Stats API",
  "endpoint": "https://api.startupstats.com/v1/startups",
  "method": "GET",
  "description": "Retrieve a list of startups with optional filters on industry, location, funding, and growth metrics.",
  "parameters": [
    {
      "name": "industry",
      "type": "string",
      "required": false,
      "description": "Filter by industry sector (e.g., \"tech\", \"healthcare\", \"fintech\")."
    },
    {
      "name": "location",
      "type": "string",
      "required": false,
      "description": "Filter by country or region (e.g., \"USA\", \"Europe\", \"Silicon Valley\")."
    },
    {
      "name": "min_funding",
      "type": "number",
      "required": false,
      "description": "Minimum total funding in USD."
    },
    {
      "name": "max_funding",
      "type": "number",
      "required": false,
      "description": "Maximum total funding in USD."
    },
    {
      "name": "min_growth_rate",
      "type": "number",
      "required": false,
      "description": "Minimum year‑over‑year revenue growth rate (percentage)."
    },
    {
      "name": "page",
      "type": "integer",
      "required": false,
      "default": 1,
      "description": "Pagination page number."
    },
    {
      "name": "per_page",
      "type": "integer",
      "required": false,
      "default": 20,
      "description": "Number of records per page."
    }
  ],
  "authentication": {
    "type": "Bearer Token",
    "header": "Authorization",
    "example": "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY"
  },
  "example_request": {
    "method": "GET",
    "url": "https://api.startupstats.com/v1/startups?industry=tech&location=USA&min_funding=5000000&page=1&per_page=10",
    "headers": {
      "Authorization": "Bearer YOUR_API_KEY",
      "Accept": "application/json"
    }
  },
  "example_response": {
    "status": 200,
    "body": {
      "meta": {
        "total_records": 1250,
        "page": 1,
        "per_page": 10,
        "total_pages": 125
      },
      "data": [
        {
          "startup_id": "abc123",
          "name": "TechNova",
          "industry": "Technology",
          "location": "San Francisco, USA",
          "founded_year": 2018,
          "total_funding_usd": 12000000,
          "revenue_last_year_usd": 2500000,
          "growth_rate_percent": 35,
          "employees": 45,
          "website": "https://technova.com"
        },
        {
          "startup_id": "def456",
          "name": "HealthPulse",
          "industry": "Healthcare",
          "location": "Boston, USA",
          "founded_year": 2019,
          "total_funding_usd": 8000000,
          "revenue_last_year_usd": 1800000,
          "growth_rate_percent": 28,
          "employees": 30,
          "website": "https://healthpulse.com"
        }
        // … 8 more records
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

### How to Use It

1. **Get an API Key** – Sign up at the provider’s portal and obtain a bearer token.
2. **Make a Request** – Include the `Authorization` header and any desired query parameters.
3. **Parse the Response** – The JSON payload contains a `meta` section for pagination and a `data` array with startup details.

Feel free to adapt the parameter names or add additional filters (e.g., `stage`, `valuation`, `founder_experience`) based on your specific needs.
